      "skill_tags": ["algebraic_fractions", "factorising"],
      "problem_text": "Simplify by factorising: $\\frac{x^2 - 4}{x^2 - 2x - 8}$",
      "answer": "$\\frac{x - 2}{x - 4}$, $x \\neq -2, 4$",
      "solution": "Numerator: $x^2-4 = (x+2)(x-2)$. Denominator: $x^2-2x-8 = (x+2)(x-4)$. Cancel $(x+2)$: $\\frac{x-2}{x-4}$, $x \\neq -2, 4$"
    },
    {
      "id": "B1_Q2_X3",
      "difficulty": "X",
      "skill_tags": ["factorising", "proof"],
      "problem_text": "Prove that $n^3 - n$ is always divisible by 6 for any integer $n$.",
      "answer": "Proof given",
      "solution": "$n^3 - n = n(n^2-1) = n(n-1)(n+1)$. This is the product of three consecutive integers, so it always contains a multiple of 2 (at least one even number) and a multiple of 3 (one of every three consecutive numbers is divisible by 3). Therefore it is divisible by $2 \\times 3 = 6$."
    },
